-- The self-hosted compiler's entry point (stage 23e). The command line is
-- `selfhost/Cli.wiz` (`dispatch`: `check`/`build`/`run`/`eval`, or, with no subcommand,
-- the one-shot tool that reads `input.wiz` and prints C).
--
-- `main` is a module of its own, named as the frontend's root module (`Main`), so the
-- program is built from checked-in source only: the tables are `selfhost/Tables.wiz`,
-- the driver is `selfhost/Cli.wiz`, and this file is last. `Wiz/Selfhost.compilerSource`
-- puts the two build identity values (`wizVersion`, `toolchainId`) before it; they are
-- the release string and a hash of these sources, i.e. data a build must pass in, not
-- Wiz code.
def main : IO Unit := do
  args ← IO.args;
  dispatch args
